component-lattice | L_cmp is the original component-class lattice Z^D/Z(1,...,1), with the identical inclusion in H^2(X). Both directions fix every component class x_i and every rational coefficient; all six later lattice uses in this primitive-extension argument keep that object.
period-matrix | M_per is the same displayed matrix [[8,24],[-6,-16]] and its inverse in the same short/long bases. Its determinant and the transfer coefficients are unchanged.
period-lattice | The period lattice is the existing L_per from PC5, generated by (8,-6),(24,-16). The name changes in its deck action, group cohomology, quotient-cusp and boundary subscripts, free resolution and component-edge congruence; all maps retain the same integer vectors and translations. The old abstract free-abelian-group notation L=Z^2 is written using the actual ordered basis: (a,b) maps to (8a+24b,-6a-16b), with inverse (x,y) maps to (-x-3y/2,3x/8+y/2) on L_per=8Z⊕2Z. This supplies the exact same two-dimensional free resolution without asserting equality of the subgroup with ambient Z^2.
