short-long-matrix | E_sl=E is the displayed short–long matrix [[1,0],[0,0]]. All affine cocycles, Thom/support differences and the final shifted-Picard-column congruence keep the same bilinear map. The cusp complement E and toric classes E_i are unchanged.
rectangle-winding | nu is the original integral transition winding denoted k in this local rectangle calculation; A_conn=A and F_conn=F are its unchanged connection and curvature. The coefficient ring k=Z/8 remains fixed everywhere. The map nu↔old integer k is identity on Z, with the displayed degree formula unchanged.
strip-constants | c_j^str=c_j are exactly the two strip constants (4,4) in k. Their affine-cocycle occurrences and equalities change names together. The Chern classes c_i(X) and later endpoint-unit functions c_i(f) are outside this scope.
