cusp-boundary-domain | The old two uses of partial U have no local definition. Q104 defines N_L as the quotient over |q|<=epsilon and M_L=partial N_L. 02LK Boundary coordinates states: 'The period exponential defined above identifies the boundary with the mapping torus of the literal return' [[I,B0],[0,I]], and 'The inverse is the real period logarithm.' 02LN's positive-weight cap applies that same fan and integral boundary maps with C=[[nu,b*kappa],[-a*kappa,w-a*b*kappa^2/nu]]. PC3 has (nu,a,b,kappa,w)=(8,2,8,3,2), so C=[[8,24],[-6,-16]], determinant16, exactly the PC5 period matrix. The permutation H=(e1,delta,e2,gamma) has inverse its transpose and H^-1 A0 H=[[I,C],[0,I]]. The period exponential/logarithm therefore identify the earlier cap U with the opening cusp N, preserving the fibre inclusion T4→partial N, the projection q→q/|q|, the positive meridian and the two fixed-loop prism sections. The fibre area alpha_partial=e1 wedge delta is the same element under this marking; its two inclusions are into N and E=X minus int(N). Thus both groups are H2(partial N); the later perturbed sphere is separately N_sph. No Wang arrow, matrix entry or kernel/image assertion changes.
